SERVICE = {
"He's Not Where You Left Him":{
"intro":"My name is ___ and I have been part of this church for ___ years. I was asked to introduce this morning and I said yes before anyone told me what it was about, which is how most of my volunteering happens here. Here is what I will tell you. There is something in my life I had quietly decided was finished. I made my peace with it a while ago and I stopped checking. This week I found out I had stopped checking too early. Some of us walked in this morning carrying spices for a funeral that is not happening. Would you welcome Pastor ___.",
"off":"Father, everything in these baskets already belongs to you. We are not funding a program this morning. We are saying out loud that we believe the tomb is empty, and that this changes what we do with what we have. Take it and spend it on people who have not heard yet. In Jesus' name, amen.",
"ben":"Go from here into a week you have already decided how it ends. Go anyway. And when you reach the thing you have been dreading, look carefully &mdash; because the God who moved a stone before anyone arrived has been working ahead of you the whole time. He is not where you left him. Go and find out.",
"night":["Write down the one ending you have accepted. Fold it. Put it where you will see it Monday morning.",
"Text one person the sentence: he is not where you left him. Do not explain it.",
"Ask someone in your house what they have stopped expecting God to do.",
"Check on the thing you have been avoiding. Make the call tonight if there is any way to make it tonight."]},

"When Mother's Day Hurts":{
"intro":"My name is ___. I want to say something before Pastor ___ comes up, and then I am going to sit down. Some of you have been dreading today for about three weeks. I know that because I have been one of you. This service is not going to walk past that. If you need to cry this morning, please do it in here, surrounded by people, rather than alone in your car afterward. And if today is a good day for you, and I hope it is, would you look around this room and notice who is quiet. Thank you. Pastor ___.",
"off":"God, some of us can barely pray this morning, so we are going to do this instead. We give because you have been near to us in seasons when nothing got fixed. Use it for the women in this city carrying more than anyone knows. Amen.",
"ben":"Go from here without pretending. You are not required to be fine, and you never were. The God who sat with Hannah on the temple floor is going home with you this afternoon. Go in his nearness.",
"night":["Tell one person the true version of how today actually went.",
"If today was easy for you, text someone for whom it was not. Do not say anything clever.",
"Eat something and go to bed early. Treat it as obedience rather than indulgence.",
"Write out the prayer you have been afraid to pray. You do not have to pray it yet."]},

"Who Are You Bringing?":{
"intro":"My name is ___. Eleven years ago somebody in this church invited me to something and I said no. Then they asked again about six months later and I said yes, mostly to end the conversation. I am standing up here now. That is the entire story. Somebody in this room is the reason somebody else is going to be in this room. Pastor ___ is going to show you how simple it actually is.",
"off":"Lord, we are giving this morning for people who are not here yet. Every dollar in these baskets is aimed at an empty seat. Make us the kind of church somebody would actually want to be brought to. Amen.",
"ben":"Go with a name in your pocket. Not a project &mdash; a person, with a whole life and a set of reasons and a Tuesday afternoon much like yours. Somebody wrote your name down once, and that is why you are here. Go be that for one person this week.",
"night":["Send the text tonight. Not tomorrow &mdash; tomorrow the resolve is gone and the name is still on the card.",
"Pray for that person out loud, by name, before you fall asleep.",
"Tell one person in your house who you wrote down, so that somebody asks you about it Wednesday.",
"Put the card where you will see it every morning this week."]},

"You Were Not Built to Do This Alone":{
"intro":"My name is ___ and I sat in this row by myself for two years. Not because anyone was unkind. This church is kind. I simply never signed up for anything, and two years went by. Then I joined a group because a woman named ___ would not stop asking me. There are four people now who would notice if I disappeared, and there were none before. That is the whole difference. That is all I have. Pastor ___.",
"off":"Father, thank you that you never intended any of us to do this alone. What we give this morning goes toward rooms, tables, and the people who lead them. Use it to make sure nobody in this church has to sit alone for two years. Amen.",
"ben":"Go, but do not go alone. There are people at the back holding signs, and there is a chair with your name on it whether or not you have taken it yet. Two are better than one. Go this week and prove it.",
"night":["If you signed up, text your group leader tonight and say hello first. Go first.",
"Name three people who would notice if you stopped coming. If you cannot reach three, that is the finding.",
"Tell one person one true thing you are carrying.",
"Put all six group dates on your calendar before you go to sleep. All six, tonight."]},

"Light in the Dark":{
"intro":"My name is ___. This is my ___ Christmas Eve in this room. I want to say one thing to whoever came tonight because somebody in your family made you come. Nobody in here is going to ask anything of you. You can sing or not sing. You can leave right after the candles and nobody will follow you into the parking lot. But something happens in this room in about twenty minutes when the lights go out, and I would hate for you to miss it. Pastor ___.",
"off":"God, on the night you came there was no room for you. Tonight we are giving so that there is room &mdash; for the family down the street who cannot cover December, for the people in this city sitting in the dark. Take it and make room. Amen.",
"ben":"Go into the dark carrying light. You were not asked to be the sun. One candle is enough and always has been, because darkness has never once put out a single flame. Merry Christmas. Go home and be one candle.",
"night":["Before anyone goes to bed, say one sentence of blessing over each person in your house. Use their names.",
"Text one person who is alone tonight. Two sentences is plenty.",
"Leave one light on and tell your children why.",
"Read John 1:1-5 out loud at the table before anyone sleeps."]},

"Do Not Rush This":{
"intro":"My name is ___. I took communion in this church for six years without thinking about it once. Six years. It was the thing that happened while I was checking whether my kids were behaving in the next row. Then about a year ago somebody handed me the bread and said my name while they did it, and I could not get through it. That is what we are doing this morning, and we are taking our time with it. Pastor ___.",
"off":"Jesus, at this table you gave everything before anyone deserved any of it. What we give now is a small echo of a very large thing. Use it for people who need bread of the ordinary kind this week. Amen.",
"ben":"Go with the taste of it still in your mouth. You proclaimed his death this morning whether or not you said a word, and you said out loud that you expect him back. Go and live this week like people who are waiting for something.",
"night":["Make the peace you thought about during the silence. Send it tonight while you still mean it.",
"Tell one person at your table what you were actually thinking about when you took the bread.",
"Set tomorrow's dinner table before you go to bed. Let it mean something.",
"Thank somebody for something before the cost rather than after it."]},
}

IMIN = {
"intro":"One QR code in the bulletin. Tap it, and thirty seconds later a person is enrolled, counted, and starting tomorrow morning. It replaces the communication card rather than sitting alongside it, which is the entire point &mdash; a church cannot report a number it never collected.",
"flow":[
("The code","Printed on the bulletin, on the screen behind the pastor, and on the back of the commitment card. Same code in all three places. People scan whichever one is nearest."),
("One screen","Name, email or phone, and which journey. Seven days, ten-day jumpstart, twenty-one day challenge, or thirty-day journey. One button underneath, and the button says <em>I'm In</em>."),
("It is the card","This replaces the communication card. Same data, collected in real time instead of on a table Monday morning. Anyone who will not scan still fills in the paper version, and the office keys those in by Tuesday."),
("The counter","A live count the pastor can see on a phone from the platform. Not a vanity metric &mdash; a pastoral one. You now know precisely how many people in your church are reading the same passage on the same morning."),
("The number, said out loud","Two weeks in: <em>as of this morning, thirty-one percent of this room has started.</em> A specific number spoken from the platform does more than any amount of urging, because it stops being an idea somebody suggested and becomes a thing your neighbors are already doing."),
("It is never too late","The arc runs from each person's own start date, not the church's. Somebody who scans in week three still gets a complete seven days. Say this every week, because most churches announce a start date and quietly treat everyone who missed it as a loss."),
],
"report":[
"How many started, by journey length.",
"How many are still going on day four &mdash; the day the drop happens, every time.",
"How many enrolled a spiritual partner through their own link.",
"How many responded at least once, which is the truest engagement number you will get.",
"How many finished, and how many of those joined a group afterward.",
],
"warn":"Report the percentage, never the names, and never from the platform in a way that makes the people who have not started feel counted against. The number is an invitation, not a scoreboard.",
}

EMAIL = {
"intro":"One template, sent every morning for seven days, with exactly one field the pastor fills in himself. Everything else is already written. Four minutes a week, and it is the difference between a congregation hearing from a church and hearing from a person.",
"anatomy":[
("From","The pastor's own name and address. Never the church office, never a no-reply. The reply-to has to go somewhere a human reads."),
("Subject","The day's devotional title. Nothing else &mdash; no series branding, no day counter in the subject line. It should read like a note, not a newsletter."),
("Line one &mdash; his","Two sentences, written by the pastor that morning or the night before. This is the only field he touches and it is the entire reason the email works."),
("The devotional","The day's reading, unchanged. About a hundred and fifty words, formatted for a phone."),
("The video","Ninety seconds, embedded as a thumbnail that opens in one tap. Never an attachment, never a link that asks anyone to log in."),
("The response","One question and an actual box. The reply goes to a real inbox and a human reads it before Thursday."),
("The footer","Tomorrow's title, in one line. People finish a thing they can see the end of."),
],
"template":"From: [Pastor's name]\\nSubject: [Day title]\\n\\n[TWO SENTENCES FROM YOU. Write these last, write them fast, and do not polish them. Say what you noticed, what you are wrestling with, or who you thought of. That is all this needs to be.]\\n\\n---\\n\\n[Day title]\\n[Passage reference, NIV]\\n\\n[The devotional reading, supplied]\\n\\nReflect: [the day's question]\\nDo: [the day's action]\\n\\n[Watch &mdash; 90 seconds]\\n\\n---\\n\\nWhat came to mind? Reply to this email. I read them, and with your permission we share some of them anonymously on Sunday to encourage the rest of the church.\\n\\nTomorrow: [next day's title]",
"rule":"If the pastor has nothing to say on a given morning, he should write that. <em>Honestly, I have nothing to add today &mdash; just read it.</em> That sentence builds more trust than four polished ones.",
}

BOOKLET = {
"case":[
"Ask a congregation what they remember from a series eighteen months later and almost nobody will quote the sermon. But a surprising number will still have the booklet in a nightstand drawer with their own handwriting in it.",
"That is the argument. A sermon is an event. A journal is an object, and objects outlive events.",
"It is also the cheapest thing a church will ever print, the easiest thing to put a church's name on, and the only piece in the entire system that a person will physically hand to someone else without being asked to.",
],
"why":[
("It gets finished","A book with twenty pages and a checkbox on each spread gets completed by people who have never finished a devotional in their lives. The finish line has to be visible."),
("It gets branded","The church's name on the cover changes what it is. It stops being curriculum somebody bought and becomes the thing our church made, which is a different object entirely."),
("It gets handed over","Nobody forwards an email to a neighbor. People hand a small book across a fence. Print an extra thirty percent and tell the congregation to give them away."),
("It gets kept","Six months later the series is forgotten and the booklet is still in the drawer, with handwriting in it, which means it is still working."),
("It becomes a product","A church that produces three of these has a line. A church with a line has something other churches will buy, and that is the point at which the printing cost stops being a cost."),
],
"custom":[
("The cover","Church name, the series title, and nothing else. Resist the logo lockup and the tagline. A cover with three words on it looks confident."),
("The welcome page","A hundred words from the pastor in first person. This is the single highest-leverage customization and it takes ten minutes to write."),
("The commitment page","Name, date, and the name of the spiritual partner. Signed in the service with a pen, which is why it must be paper."),
("The tracker","A grid of days to check off, on page three, before any content. Progress has to be visible without flipping."),
("The back page","Group signup, the QR code, and the date of the Celebration Sunday. Never leave the back page blank &mdash; it is the most-looked-at page in the book."),
],
}
